036 <= 0 is precise and null in the claimed direction (R15 upper bound 0.144), and H25 shows no high-signature reverse effect (R16 upper bound 0.130). Thus the evidence suggests a tail-specific rather than gradient-like signal if it is real. H11 remains unresolved and active because its point estimate crosses the threshold but uncertainty and subgroup-selection risk are material; I request independent validation for H11 rather than H19 or H17, because H19/H17 have intervals far from the decision boundary while H11 is threshold- and selection-sensitive. H13 and H14 do not support feature_007 or feature_015 as drivers of the low-feature_036 signal; H14 is closed, and H13 is deferred as a weak specificity check. H23 shows a precise null direct feature_007 contrast within feature_058=0 (upper bound 0.110), so I close H23 and also close H4: the marker-marker interaction line is not supported by an absolute stratum contrast. The broad screens produce a near-threshold feature_003 effect (R18 point 0.141, interval 0.062 to 0.220), which remains active but unresolved; feature_001 and feature_035 are precise nulls and closed. Competing explanations include true predictor associations in this dataset, correlated predictors sharing latent outcome structure, chance subgroup selection in the feature_036 tail, and multiple testing; the proposed validation and follow-ups are intended to separate these.",
