  "narrative": "The new conditional analyses strongly reinforce the two accepted measured associations. H39 estimates feature_010=1 versus feature_010=0 within feature_037=0 as signed +0.444 with 95% CI +0.346 to +0.542 (R24), and H40 does so within feature_037=1 as +0.412 with CI +0.206 to +0.618 (R25). H41 estimates feature_037=1 versus feature_037=0 within feature_010=0 as +0.833 with CI +0.779 to +0.887 (R26), and H42 estimates it within feature_010=1 as +0.865 with CI +0.644 to +1.086 (R27). All four point estimates and interval lower bounds exceed the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction, so I accept them as dataset-internal associations. The similarity across strata argues against attenuation of one effect by conditioning on the other and is more consistent with two largely independent or additively associated predictor axes than with one marker simply proxying the other. These are still not causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claims; they are robust within the supplied dataset, possibly reflecting shared latent structure or dataset construction.\n\nThe feature_003 conditional evidence is suggestive but not threshold-supported. H43 in feature_037=0 gives +0.133 with CI +0.056 to +0.210 (R28); H44 in feature_010=0 gives +0.125 with CI +0.051 to +0.199 (R29); H47 in feature_037=1 gives +0.140 with CI -0.028 to +0.308 (R30); H48 in feature_010=1 gives +0.199 with CI -0.053 to +0.452 (R31); and the joint baseline stratum feature_037=0 and feature_010=0, H49, gives +0.135 with CI +0.064 to +0.206 (R32). None has a lower confidence bound above 0.15, and most point estimates fall just below the threshold. H48 is the only point estimate above threshold, but its interval is wide, includes no association, and arises in a smaller stratum after multiple conditional tests, so it cannot be accepted. Therefore I defer H43, H44, H47, and H48. H49 remains unresolved and active because it is the most direct baseline-conditioned test and its upper interval still exceeds the threshold, but the central question is whether feature_003 has any independent association that would survive external validation.\n\nThe broad screens H50-H52 are not scientifically supported. H50 feature_047 is small and imprecise with CI upper bound below threshold (R33); H51 feature_016 is signed in the opposite direction of its claim with an interval essentially spanning null and not exceeding threshold (R34); H52 feature_013 is centered near zero with CI upper below threshold (R35). I reject and close those three exact comparisons.\n\nI request independent validation of H15, the main feature_003 claim, rather than one of the smaller conditional strata. H15 is the least subgroup-selected version of the feature_003 hypothesis and has the most usable discovery signal: signed +0.141 with CI +0.062 to +0.220 (R18). Validation is decision-relevant because feature_003 is consistently near, but below, the threshold and all intervals include effects below 0.15. If independent validation fails to support a threshold-exceeding association, I would reject H15 and close or defer the feature_003 conditional line unless a separate strong effect appears. If it succeeds, H15/H49 would support a modest but scientifically meaningful feature_003 association, with interpretation still limited to association rather than causality.",
