  "narrative": "The eight robustness contrasts materially strengthen the two already supported dataset-internal associations. For feature_037, the dependency-increasing effect remains very large across clinically interpretable natural-log PFS strata: H53 in low feature_040 gives +0.760 with 95% CI +0.614 to +0.906 (R38), and H54 in high feature_040 gives +0.830 with CI +0.699 to +0.962 (R39). It is also large across feature_019 low/high strata: H57 gives +0.889 with CI +0.787 to +0.991 (R42), and H58 gives +0.773 with CI +0.660 to +0.886 (R43). All four point estimates and lower bounds exceed the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction, so I accept these exact subgroup contrasts as dataset-internal robustness evidence and close them as exact comparisons. These are not causal or generalizable mechanistic claims, but they make it much less likely that feature_037 is an isolated artifact of one unadjusted analysis.\n\nFor feature_010, the weaker-dependency/higher-outcome association is also robust in most strata. H55 in low feature_040 gives +0.501 with CI +0.317 to +0.684 (R40); H59 in low feature_019 gives +0.510 with CI +0.349 to +0.671 (R44); and H60 in high feature_019 gives +0.407 with CI +0.260 to +0.553 (R45). I accept and close those exact subgroup claims. The high feature_040 stratum H56 is different: the point estimate is +0.290 with CI +0.068 to +0.511 (R41), so the central estimate exceeds the threshold, but the lower confidence bound does not. The evidence supports a positive association in that subgroup, perhaps with attenuation, but is not precise enough to conclude threshold-exceeding association with high confidence. I therefore leave H56 unresolved and active rather than accepting the exact threshold claim.\n\nThe new binary screens mostly produced nulls. H18 feature_048 is essentially null: +0.008 with CI -0.068 to +0.085 (R46); reject and close. H20 feature_023 is small and in the opposite direction of the registered claim: signed -0.058 with CI -0.130 to +0.014 (R47); reject and close. H22 feature_031 has a small positive signal, +0.107 with CI +0.035 to +0.178 (R49), below the 0.15-unit threshold and not promising enough to justify continued follow-up, so I reject and close the exact screen.\n\nThe important unexpected result is H21 feature_002. Registered in the dependency-increasing direction, it produced a large opposite signed effect: -0.832 with CI -0.897 to -0.766 (R48). Thus the exact H21 claim is rejected and closed, but the data strongly suggest a large opposite dataset association: feature_002=1 versus 0 may be associated with higher outcome values/weaker composite dependency. I registered a reversed main claim plus conditional stratum claims to test whether this is likely independent of the already accepted feature_037 and feature_010 axes or merely correlated with them. The large magnitude and tight interval make feature_002 a high-priority follow-up, but it still requires formal registration as the opposite direction and ideally validation.\n\nI request independent validation of H34, the main feature_010 association. It is accepted on discovery evidence and now shows robustness across feature_037, feature_010, feature_019, and most feature_040 strata, but it has not yet been independently validated. This is more useful than validating an accepted subgroup contrast because a successful validation would support the central feature_010 association rather than only a selected stratum.",
