  "narrative": "H122 response deadline is now satisfied. The discovery contrast was +0.921 with signed lower bound +0.733, and independent validation R130 was +0.799 with signed lower bound +0.527. Both are in the registered attenuation direction and exceed the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold, with the validation interval adjusted for the run's maximum number of validation comparisons. I therefore accept and close H122. This strengthens the conclusion that the feature_010 exposure-comparator contrast is substantially lower in the feature_038>=0 assay context than in its complement, after the broad eligibility screen on feature_018. Because feature_038 and feature_018 are correlated constructed standardized assays, this should be interpreted as joint assay-tail heterogeneity, not as independent causal modification by either assay alone.\n\nFinal supported dataset-internal pattern. The strongest reproducible main-axis associations are: (1) feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001, approximately 0.80 to 0.83 units lower, indicating stronger composite dependency in this assay-positive group; this is validated by H19/R37. (2) feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 globally, about 0.42 units higher, indicating weaker composite dependency; this is validated by H34/R50. (3) feature_002=1 is associated with higher outcome_001, about 0.85 units higher, also indicating weaker dependency; this is validated by H70/R63. These are associations within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, pathway membership, or external generalizability.\n\nThe most important context-dependent finding is that the global positive feature_010 association attenuates and locally reverses in joint nonnegative feature_038/feature_018 assay contexts. Validated attenuation interactions include H110, H120, H122, and H141; accepted but discovery-only summary and related interactions include H150, H142, H111, H117, H119, and H121. The absolute sign-stratum contrasts are coherent: H151, H152, and H153 show that the feature_010 contrast remains large and positive when at least one of feature_038 or feature_018 is negative, whereas H149 and H158 show that it is strongly negative when both assay tails are nonnegative. H158 further indicates that the local reversal is not simply a feature_002-positive mixture because it persists when eligibility is restricted to feature_002=0. H150 should be treated as a compact arithmetic summary of the same feature_010 sign-stratum contrasts rather than as independent confirmation.\n\nSpecificity is supported for feature_037 and feature_002. The lower outcome_001 contrast for feature_037=1 and the higher outcome_001 contrast for feature_002=1 persist across many assay-tail contexts, including asymmetric contexts where exactly one of feature_038 or feature_018 is nonnegative, and in the triple nonnegative assay context where feature_038>=0, feature_018>=0, and feature_036>=0. Therefore the assay-context heterogeneity is relatively specific to the feature_010 contrast rather than reflecting a collapse of all main associations in the joint positive assay region. This remains an unadjusted, dataset-internal specificity observation.\n\nNegative and boundary findings. The initially investigated feature_058/feature_036 tail hypothesis is not supported: the promising discovery subgroup estimate H11 failed independent validation, and H24 reversed direction in validation. feature_003 is statistically detectable in some settings but not scientifically meaningful by the 0.15-unit threshold and failed validation in the feature_037=0 and feature_010=0 stratum. Direct interaction tests among the strongest main axes, including feature_010 with feature_037 and feature_002 with feature_010, feature_037, feature_018, and feature_038, were mostly near null or failed validation, including H45/H46, H88, H123/H124, H125/H126, H127/H128, H139/H140, and H144. Many binary and categorical screens were null or did not reach the absolute threshold, including the recently completed broad screens H32, H33, and H64.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. feature_063 remains borderline and unresolved: H27's signed lower bound is +0.131, below the 0.15 threshold. Attribution between feature_038 and feature_018 remains unresolved because they are correlated constructed assays and the registered comparisons are unadjusted. Several registered predictor screens and context-specific follow-ups remain unresolved or untested, including H65, H66, H82, H98, H99, H108, H109, H159, H160, and H161. No independent validation requests remain, so any future findings will be discovery-internal unless scheduled validation is delivered.\n\nMost informative next analyses. With H122 closed, the next highest-value work is to sharpen specificity and reduce redundancy among correlated contexts. Prioritize registered H161, which tests whether the local feature_010 reversal in the joint nonnegative assay context persists after removing feature_037=1. Then test H159 and H160, the feature_037 and feature_002 contrasts in the joint nonnegative assay context, to confirm that the main-axis specificity pattern is not an artifact of a single assay or subgroup. If slots remain, test lower-priority active broad screens H65, H66, H82, H98, H99, H108, and H109. Interpret all accepted associations as dataset-internal composite-score associations only, not as causal effects, mechanistic relationships, gene-level knockout biology, clinical associations, or generalizable findings.",
  "research_notes": "H122 accepted and closed on independent validation. Final dataset-internal model: feature_037=1 -> lower outcome_001; feature_010=1 -> higher outcome_001 globally; feature_002=1 -> higher outcome_001. The feature_010 association is strongly context-dependent: positive in at least one negative assay context (H151-H153), negative in joint nonnegative feature_038/feature_018 context (H149, H158), with validated attenuation summaries H110, H120, H122, H141. H150 is summary arithmetic, not independent replication. feature_038 and feature_018 should be described jointly because they are correlated constructed assays. feature_037 and feature_002 show relative specificity by persisting across assay contexts and triple nonnegative context. Negative/boundary: feature_058/feature_036 tail unstable, H11 validation failure and H24 reversal; feature_003 below threshold or validation fails; direct main-axis interactions mostly null. Unresolved: feature_063 H27 below threshold, assay attribution between feature_038/018, and active screens/follow-ups H65, H66, H82, H98, H99, H108, H109, H159-H161. Next analyze priority: H161 first to remove feature_037, then H159/H160 for feature_037/002 specificity in joint positive assay context; then pending broad screens. No validation requests remain. All conclusions are dataset-internal associations, not causality, mechanism, biology, or generalizability."
