  "narrative": "Final synthesis at iteration 22/25. No new validation response or response deadline is present, assessments_due is empty, and independent-validation capacity is exhausted. I therefore do not force any new status changes in this synthesis step; the controller-maintained accepted claim set remains based on the accumulated discovery and validation evidence. The main scientific report is below.\n\nSUPPORTED DATASET-INTERNAL FINDINGS.\n1. feature_037=1 is the clearest robust lower-outcome axis. The signed global contrast is +0.833 [0.767, 0.898] in discovery and +0.800 [0.706, 0.895] in independent validation. Because the registered direction is -1, positive signed estimates indicate feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001, i.e. stronger composite dependency. This lower-outcome association was accepted across major strata and remained threshold-supported after excluding the rare feature_027 population. It is therefore supported as a primary dataset-internal association, not as a causal or biological effect.\n\n2. feature_002=1 is the clearest robust higher-outcome axis. The signed global contrast is +0.832 [0.766, 0.897] in discovery and +0.851 [0.756, 0.945] in validation. This direction is opposite to feature_037. It survived exclusion of feature_027 and remained threshold-supported across many primary and secondary strata. The primary feature_002 and feature_037 axes therefore appear mutually robust rather than simple artifacts of one another or of rare secondary signals.\n\n3. feature_010=1 is globally higher-outcome but strongly context dependent. The signed global contrast is +0.423 [0.327, 0.520] in discovery and +0.421 [0.293, 0.549] in validation. However, in nonnegative feature_038 and feature_018 assay-tail contexts, feature_010 shows a lower-outcome pattern relative to its complement. This is supported by several validated interactions and mean contrasts, including H110, H120, H122, H141, and the threshold-shift panel H249-H252. The